    "type": "bugfix",
    "problem": [
      {
        "text": "Ernie 4.5 routed experts previously requested FP16 gate/up outputs. The change widens these intermediates to FP32, without widening the activation output supplied to the down projection.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_26c9e703f630491183d18710c92d0226",
          "call_9bb5901c23cf4d2cbcf2fa17cd590959"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "reasoning": [
      {
        "text": "The likely numerical purpose is to avoid premature overflow or precision loss before SiLU multiplication. This is an interpretation of the dtype change and existing kernels, not a demonstrated Ernie failure or measured accuracy improvement.",
        "basis": "inference",
        "evidence": [
          "call_26c9e703f630491183d18710c92d0226",
          "call_cb38fd2160a1487abdcebcebd57246f1",
          "call_2c2fe27dfc0141e58ae6e1fd1eb8346c"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "impact": [
      {
        "text": "Only routed-expert intermediates change. Dense-prefix and shared-expert GatedMLPs retain FP16 intermediates; routed down-projection outputs remain FP32. Routing and ordinary-versus-fused expert selection are unchanged.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_26c9e703f630491183d18710c92d0226",
          "call_e30418cfab4a4e4eb44dc412f544c414",
          "call_9bb5901c23cf4d2cbcf2fa17cd590959"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "source_notes": [
      {
        "text": "Read the Ernie introduction entry. It establishes the reused dense-prefix/routed/shared assembly and records conditional fused-path limitations; the current source and one-line diff retain those forward-path limitations.",
        "basis": "ancestor",
        "evidence": [
          "call_aba8f749bdc248e0a26735f6fcf0bb97",
          "call_f8644eef60684af2adb507cb3debf820"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The inspected discussions are background, not established motivation. #34, \u201ctorch._C._LinAlgError on last layer of quant,\u201d concerns Command-A conversion; #42, \u201cconverting to 3.0 bpw causes error; block state has 0 inf values and 34 NaN values,\u201d concerns Midnight-Miqu and Command-R+; #52, \u201cError converting moonshotai/Kimi-Dev-72B,\u201d discusses widening down outputs; #53, \u201cCommand A support,\u201d begins as a support request and later reports conversion failures; #58, \u201clinalg.cholesky error converting OpenBuddy (Qwen3) 32B QAT,\u201d reports another model's NaNs. Their inferred connection is the shared Linear conversion traceback and numerical-overflow theme, not evidence that this Ernie intermediate change fixes them.",
        "basis": "inference",
        "evidence": [
          "call_5f4381eb1f8b4b4da300b59d742eb6b1",
          "call_534b040efc4942d29bfec70bfb1873bc",
          "call_1a4cfb12869647b6bf9ae74660a9aa3c",
          "call_1dbb82cd7dea4a7e9956d54452f8213b",
          "call_d2c522edab494833a719821032befa1f",
          "call_cb38b10d7b4b4b93a0785e3eb6dfb060",
