    "chapters": [
      {
        "id": "models",
        "title": "Widen routed-expert gate/up intermediates",
        "claims": [
          {
            "text": "Ernie4_5MoEModel.__init__ changes the BlockSparseMLP interm_dtype argument from torch.half to torch.float. The dense-prefix boundary remains idx < first_k_dense_replace; optional shared experts are separately constructed GatedMLPs and are not widened.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_26c9e703f630491183d18710c92d0226",
              "call_e30418cfab4a4e4eb44dc412f544c414"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "BlockSparseMLP passes interm_dtype to every routed gate/up Linear as out_dtype. Linear forwards that setting into its loaded backend. For ordinary FP16 weights, LinearFP16 allocates the requested output dtype; half input with float output selects ext.hgemm, whose float-output branch uses half operands, FP32 output and CUBLAS_COMPUTE_32F. This changes intermediate/output arithmetic, not checkpoint weight storage.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_9bb5901c23cf4d2cbcf2fa17cd590959",
              "call_ee238510cafb4ee0940f4e751840a1c7",
              "call_de2c0a906467402b970f52be4f073eba",
              "call_2c2fe27dfc0141e58ae6e1fd1eb8346c"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The existing non-half path supplies the necessary activation destination: ordinary expert evaluation allocates a separate half tensor, and load allocates half interm_a separately from float interm_g/interm_u. silu_mul requires float gate/up inputs together and always requires a half destination. Its float kernel computes SiLU and multiplication in float, then converts the product to half. Thus 'FP32 intermediate' does not mean the entire expert MLP becomes FP32.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_9bb5901c23cf4d2cbcf2fa17cd590959",
              "call_cb38fd2160a1487abdcebcebd57246f1"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "For one flattened token with fully EXL3 experts, the fused calls write gate/up results into the widened workspaces. exl3_mgemm accepts half input with either half or float output and selects its FP32-output kernel table when C is float. Kernel availability remains shape-dependent, and the selector rejects unsupported shapes; this edit does not relax those preconditions.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_9bb5901c23cf4d2cbcf2fa17cd590959",
              "call_c6b09d65d1e342159ef136fe6984fcac",
              "call_b142536e9118465f9666c85c00bc348b",
              "call_5cb6f41c842d4a63b98670a75c2f254c",
              "call_8fa4962e69cf488ebc4cf6527ad8043b"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "All four baidu/ERNIE-4.5-21B-A3B configurations were read individually: Base-PT, Base-Paddle, PT and Paddle. Each names the changed architecture and specifies 28 layers, one dense-prefix layer, expert width 1536, 64 experts, six selected experts and two shared experts. Each therefore maps to 27 widened routed blocks while retaining half shared intermediates. None of these configurations supplies the new runtime intermediate dtype; the builder chooses it.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_96b2d50f7bd440be9df573238fc8d83c",
              "call_78109e98fdb74bdf9eceb1be6e8a849f",
              "call_b8aae398b1414b199260141ab5c3b84e",
              "call_9c8bb3ccd33140cf971a2f22a8be1f46",
              "call_e30418cfab4a4e4eb44dc412f544c414",
              "call_26c9e703f630491183d18710c92d0226"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "All seven baidu/ERNIE-4.5-300B-A47B configurations were read individually: Base-PT, Base-Paddle, PT, Paddle, 2Bits-Paddle, FP8-Paddle and W4A8C8-TP4-Paddle. Each names the changed architecture and specifies 54 layers, a three-layer dense prefix, expert width 3584, 64 experts and eight selected experts. Each omits shared-expert count, selecting the builder's zero default, and maps structurally to 51 widened routed blocks. The three quantized Paddle configurations additionally declare distinct quantization schemes; the dtype edit does not implement those formats.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_cb18de47b20e4745b80d5436ec9234a1",
              "call_61ae3ba7c1d64afba890e44c9767621a",
              "call_3f76f98954634b4fa5e512ea90d8cf33",
              "call_795792562e844bd3a69ba8e24eca4bd5",
              "call_04d9c505d9ed48c48c46fd1d25f08761",
              "call_0dc04bc5bd834b90972344c4a666cd40",
              "call_ae95f05320d0430d87b710f3d7ec374d",
              "call_e30418cfab4a4e4eb44dc412f544c414",
              "call_26c9e703f630491183d18710c92d0226"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "A bounded scalar illustration used gate=70000 and a half-rounded up value near 0.001. Rounding the gate to half first overflowed; retaining it through float SiLU multiplication produced a half output of 70.0. Workspace arithmetic also gave gate/up/activation storage of 36,864 \u2192 92,160 bytes for six experts of width 1536, and 114,688 \u2192 286,720 bytes for eight experts of width 3584. These count only those three buffers: the old activation aliases up, whereas the new activation is separate.",
            "basis": "execution",
            "evidence": [
              "call_6ad39a974bdc4fdbbc9d4110788d919e"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Wider intermediates trade extra workspace and float computation for avoiding premature half rounding. The final activation still narrows to half, so the change cannot guarantee finite results when the actual SiLU product exceeds half range. The inspected TransformerBlock immediately adds the sparse result to its residual and supplies no per-call dtype override.",
            "basis": "inference",
            "evidence": [
              "call_cb38fd2160a1487abdcebcebd57246f1",
              "call_9bb5901c23cf4d2cbcf2fa17cd590959",
              "call_525b13d730af439e9477d68a158cef78"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
